@*
    STEP 19.1: Register the model class (ProductDTO) in the 'Edit.cshtml' view to bind the form fields to the properties of the ProductDTO class.
    'Edit.cshtml' view is responsible to give facility to register new product with in the system. 
    The model class (ProductDTO) is used to represent the data structure of the product being created. 
    By registering the model class in the view, we can bind the form fields to the properties of the ProductDTO class, 
    allowing us to capture user input and create a new product object when the form is submitted.
*@
@{
}
@*STEP 19.1: Register the model class (ProductDTO) in the Edit.cshtml view to bind the form fields to the properties of the ProductDTO class
      We need it because we need to bind witht the form (Edit.cshtml) fields to the properties of the ProductDTO class.
*@
@model BestStoreMVC.Models.ProductDTO
@*STEP 19.2:Add the Form body of Edit.cshtml*@
@*Step19.2.1: Create a row*@
<div class="row">
    @*Step19.2.1.1: 
        1. col-md-8:=> This class is used to define a column that takes up 8 out of 12 columns in a medium-sized (md) viewport or larger.
        2. mx-auto:=> This class is used to center the column horizontally within its parent container. It applies automatic left and right margins to the column, effectively 'centering it on the page'.
        3. rounded:=> This class is used to apply 'rounded corner's to the column, giving it a softer and more visually appealing appearance.
        4. border:=> This class is used to add a 'border'' around the column, providing a visual separation from the surrounding content.
        5. p-3:=> This class is used to add 'padding'' of 3 units (usually 1rem) to all sides of the column, creating space between the content and the border.
    *@
    <div class="col-md-8 mx-auto rounded border p-3">
        @*Step19.2.1.1.1: Create a heading for the page that says "Edit Product" and center it using Bootstrap classes. Add a margin-bottom of 4 units to the heading.
        1. h2:=> This is an HTML heading element that represents a level 2 heading. It is used to display the title of the page, which is "Create New Product" in this case.    
        2. text-center:=> This class is used to center the text horizontally within the heading element.
        3. mb-5:=> This class is used to add a margin-bottom of 5 units (usually 3rem) to the heading, creating space between the heading and the form below it.
        *@
        <h2 class="text-center mb-5">Edit Product</h2>
        @*
            Step19.2.1.1.2:=>
            1. asp-action="Create":=> This attribute specifies the action method in the controller that will handle the form submission. 
                                      In this case, it is set to "Create", which means that when the form is submitted, it will be sent to the "Create" action method in the corresponding controller.
            2. method="post":=> This attribute specifies the HTTP method to be used when submitting the form.
            3. enctype="multipart/form-data":=> This attribute specifies the encoding type (multipart/form-data) for the form data.
        *@
        <form asp-action="Edit" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">

            @*STEP 20.4:Need to add the ID fields in the Edit.cshtml view *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">ID</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <input class="form-control-plaintext" readonly value="@ViewData["ProductId"]" />
                </div>
            </div>

            @*
                 Step19.2.1.1.3:=> For the Field name ="Name" of ProductDTO class, we need to create a form group with label, input field, and validation message.
                   1. <div class="mb-3">:=> This class is used to create a margin-bottom of 3 units (usually 1rem) for each form group, providing spacing between the input fields.
                   2. class="col-sm-4 col-form-label":=> This class is used to style the label element as a form label and specify that it should take up 4 columns in a small-sized (sm) viewport or larger. 
                        It also applies appropriate styling and spacing to the label.
                   3. class="form-control":=> This class is used to style the input element as a form control, applying appropriate styling and spacing.
                   4. asp-for:=> This attribute is used to bind the input field to a specific property of the model (ProductDTO). 
                        It automatically generates the appropriate name and id attributes for the input field based on the property name.
                   5. <span asp-validation-for="Name" class="text-danger">:=> This span element is used to display validation error messages for the "Name" property. 
                        The asp-validation-for attribute binds the span to the corresponding property, and the class="text-danger" applies a red color to the error message.
            *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">Name</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <input class="form-control" asp-for="Name" />
                    <span asp-validation-for="Name" class="text-danger"></span>
                </div>
            </div>
            @*
                Step19.2.1.1.4:=> For the Field name ="Brand" of ProductDTO class, we need to create a form group with label, input field, and validation message.
            *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">Brand</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <input class="form-control" asp-for="Brand" />
                    <span asp-validation-for="Brand" class="text-danger"></span>
                </div>
            </div>
            @*
                Step19.2.1.1.5:=> For the Field name ="Category" of ProductDTO class, we need to create a form group with label, input field, and validation message.
                Selection of category is done by using <select> tag with <option> tags for each category.

                1. class="col-sm-4 col-form-label":=> This class is used to style the label element as a form label and specify that it should take up 4 columns in a small-sized (sm) viewport or larger. 
                    It also applies appropriate styling and spacing to the label.
                2. <select asp-for="Category" class="form-select">:=> This is a select element that allows the user to choose a category from a dropdown list. 
                    The asp-for attribute binds the select element to the "Category" property of the model (ProductDTO). 
                    The class="form-select" applies Bootstrap styling to the select element.
            *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">Category</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <select asp-for="Category" class="form-select">
                        <option value="">Select a category</option>
                        <option value="Wireless Mouse">Wireless Mouse</option>
                        <option value="Bluetooth Headphones">Bluetooth Headphones</option>
                        <option value="Smartphone">Smartphone</option>
                        <option value="Gaming Laptop">Gaming Laptop</option>
                        <option value="4K Monitor">4K Monitor</option>
                    </select>
                    <span asp-validation-for="Category" class="text-danger"></span>
                </div>
            </div>

            @*
                Step19.2.1.1.6:=> For the Field name ="Price" of ProductDTO class, we need to create a form group with label, input field, and validation message.
            *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">Price</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <input class="form-control" asp-for="Price" />
                    <span asp-validation-for="Price" class="text-danger"></span>
                </div>
            </div>
            @*
                Step19.2.1.1.7:=> For the Field name ="Description" of ProductDTO class, we need to create a form group with label, input field, and validation message.
            *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">Description</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <textarea class="form-control" asp-for="Description"></textarea>
                    <span asp-validation-for="Description" class="text-danger"></span>
                </div>
            </div>

            @*
                STEP 20.4:Need to add the ImageFileName fields in the Edit.cshtml view 
                class="row col-sm-8":=> This class is used to create a new row in the Bootstrap grid system, allowing us to place the image and its label side by side.
                1. <div class="offset-sm-4 col-sm-8">:=> This class is used to create a column that takes up 8 out of 12 columns in a small-sized (sm) viewport or larger, and it is offset by 4 columns to the right. 
                    This effectively centers the image within the row.
                *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">               
                <div class="offset-sm-4 col-sm-8">
                    <img src="/Products_Images/@ViewData["ImageFileName"]" width="150" />
                </div>
            </div>
            @*
                Step19.2.1.1.8:=> For the Field name ="Image" of ProductDTO class, we need to create a form group with label, input field, and validation message.
                1. class="col-sm-4 col-form-label":=> This class is used to style the label element as a form label and specify that it should take up 4 columns in a small-sized (sm) viewport or larger. 
                    It also applies appropriate styling and spacing to the label.
                2. <input asp-for="ImageFile" type="file" class="form-control" />:=> This is an input element of type "file" that allows the user to select a file from their device.
            *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">Product Image</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <input asp-for="ImageFile" type="file" class="form-control" />
                    <span asp-validation-for="ImageFile" class="text-danger"></span>
                </div>
            </div>

            @*STEP 20.4:Need to add the CreatedAt fields in the Edit.cshtml view *@
            <div class="row col-sm-8">
                <label class="col-sm-4 col-form-label">CreatedAt</label>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <input class="form-control-plaintext" readonly value="@ViewData["CreatedAt"]" />
                </div>
            </div>
            
            @* 
                Step19.2.1.1.9:=>Add the following Buttons to the form: Submit and Cancel buttons. 
                The Submit button will submit the form data to the server, while the Cancel button will redirect the user back to the Index page of the Products controller.
                1. <div class="row">:=> This class is used to create a new row in the Bootstrap grid system, allowing us to place the buttons side by side.
                2. <div class="offset-sm-4 col-sm-4 d-grid">:=> This class is used to create a column that takes up 4 out of 12 columns.
                3. <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>:=> This is a submit button that will trigger the form submission when clicked. 
                    The class="btn btn-primary" applies Bootstrap styling to the button, giving it a primary color and appearance.
                4. <a asp-action="Index" role="button" asp-controller="Products" class="btn btn-outline-primary">:=> This is a link that acts as a button, redirecting the user to the Index action of the Products controller when clicked. 
                    The class="btn btn-outline-primary" applies Bootstrap styling to the link, giving it an outlined primary color and appearance.
            *@
            <div class="row  col-sm-8">
                <div class="offset-sm-4 col-sm-4 d-grid">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-4 d-grid">
                    <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Index" role="button">Cancel</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </form>
    </div>
</div>